# Verified fast path (hard gate)

**Do not write or propose custom code until this gate passes.**

Ask, then **use the answer**:

> Is there a better, faster, more efficient way to complete this task?

If **yes** → drop the slower plan and take that path.  
If **no** → say why this is already the fastest **safe verified** path (docs + GitHub or installed types).

Do **not** go requirement → custom implementation. Do **not** skip dashboard, CLI, prebuilt modules, or official examples because training data “already knows.”

Companions: `ponytail.mdc` (smallest diff **after** the path is chosen) · `fastest.mdc` (repeat the question once per phase) · `/fastest` (research table, no edits).

## MUST use before custom code (stop at first fit)

| # | Path | Must |
| -- | -- | -- |
| 1 | **Existing iPix / Lumina** | `graphify query` this repo; COPY+CLEAN Lumina screens/domain. Never copy old Worker auth, old CopilotKit route, or `/home/sk/ipix/app/src/mastra` wholesale. |
| 2 | **Dashboard / native feature** | Supabase Auth/RLS/extensions; Cloudinary presets/transforms/triggers; Stripe Checkout/webhooks; CopilotKit Inspector; Mastra Studio. Config over code when it fully solves it. |
| 3 | **Official CLI** | `supabase`, `stripe`, Cloudinary CLI, vendor scaffold. No custom script if a CLI command exists. |
| 4 | **Installed / prebuilt module** | `package.json` + `node_modules` types/source. No wrapper if the SDK already exports the function. Installed version beats blogs. |
| 5 | **Official docs** | **Fetch/MCP-check** current docs. API, auth, limits, recommended vs deprecated. |
| 6 | **Official GitHub repo** | **Open it.** Not archived. Examples/types match installed major. |
| 7 | **Official examples / templates / recipes / tutorials** | Adapt these before infrastructure. |
| 8 | OSS reference | Only after official/native. License, maintenance, security. |
| 9 | Smallest adapter | Thin wrap around the official feature. |
| 10 | Custom | **Last.** Only when rungs 1–9 are **proven** insufficient. |

Wait for the user if the faster path changes product scope, costs money, weakens auth, writes **production** Supabase, or drops something they asked for.

## MUST verify (critical information)

Load-bearing claims (API names, versions, auth/RLS, env keys, URLs, webhooks, signed uploads, tenant keys) are **UNVERIFIED** until checked against **current official docs** **and** **official GitHub or installed types**. Prefer a third source when it exists (live dashboard / read-only schema).

Trust-boundary work (auth, payments, isolation, persistence, media signing, webhooks, production writes): **two strong sources minimum**.

Never combined `npm run dev`. Never mutate production Supabase. No blogs as SSOT.

**100% correct** is not a research claim. Use:

| State | Meaning |
| -- | -- |
| **UNVERIFIED** | Docs/GitHub not opened, or sources disagree |
| **VERIFIED DESIGN** | Official docs + installed/GitHub agree |
| **IMPLEMENTED** | Code/config exists |
| **PROVEN** | Targeted tests pass |
| **DONE** | Real workflow + required negative/security tests + CI + evidence |

Every implement/plan task: **Correctness confidence: XX/100**.  
**100/100 only when:** official docs verified · installed or GitHub API verified · live config/schema if relevant · positive test · negative/security test · workflow/browser/CLI proof · CI · no blocking review. Else score below 100 and name the gap.

